 'QNFO.INFRA; charter pillar core; roadmap row RM-TP-3-FOOTPRINT-TEARDOWN; metric it should move: worker_count -1 (personal-watch), the design also serves any later hostname fold. Read 2026-11-05 (W2-E): personal-watch is 12 KB, binds nothing, has no cron, no secret and no inbound edge except docs and scripts/attach-watch-q08-route.py (fleet graph impact depth 3); its public address is watch.q08.org, a zone route the attach script created (ci-status/attach-watch-q08-route.json, verified true). The fold kit routes a member by path prefix on the host (--prefix, --public, --public-route), so a worker that serves its pages at the hostname root cannot be folded without moving its hostname behind a prefix. q08-mind is not a candidate for the kit: it is a multi-module bundle (WRANGLER-ONLY marker, data/entries-a.json and entries-b.json imported as modules). Work in scripts/fold_worker.py: add --host <hostname> (repeatable): the generated wrapper sends a request whose hostname equals it to the member with the path unchanged and no binding props (a public member), health still on the prefix; the generated suite proves the host routing (a request for the hostname reaches the member, any other hostname reaches the host), and a guest that is not stateless (a binding, a secret, a cron) is refused with --host unless --allow-bindings is named. Then the hostname moves with a zone route repoint (a cf-ops-actions action that PUTs the existing route id to the host script, with the old pattern kept and a revert): the host deploys first, the route moves second, the script is deleted last, and the registry row follows (migration like WORKER-COUNT-1.3). Test (no network): the generated wrapper for a fake guest answers the hostname request from the member and a foreign hostname from the host. Prediction: scripts/fold_worker.py --dry-run personal-watch personal-api --host watch.q08.org reports no refusal and the generated suite passes. Closing marker: the change carries the text FOLD-HOST-ROUTE-1.' || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=scripts/fold_worker.py' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: def plane_check(guest, host, gt, ht, keys, env_map):' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["scripts/fold_worker.py"],"contains":"FOLD-HOST-ROUTE-1"}',
 'session:W2-E', 'code', 'low', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE instr(title, 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.INFRA WORKER-COUNT-1.10:') = 1 AND status = 'open');
